    "methods_description": "MEG data were acquired using a CTF system at the Rotman Research Institute, Baycrest Hospital, Toronto. Participants performed a picture-word interference task across 3 runs of 120 trials each, with equal representation of phonologically related, semantically related, and unrelated picture-word conditions. Behavioral responses (reaction time and accuracy) were recorded via button press. Structural MRI was acquired for each participant to enable MEG source localization. MEG data were epoched relative to picture onset and response onset for event-related analyses.",
